PicoTuner (USB) support for BATC longmynd - applied by mkimage.sh after it
clones https://github.com/BritishAmateurTelevisionClub/longmynd, and by
openhamshack-apply-update to the clone already in /opt/longmynd on an existing box.

The PicoTuner's USB firmware (https://github.com/g4eml/PicoTuner, v0.12)
imitates the FT2232H's MPSSE commands, so longmynd drives it unchanged once it
will open 2E8A:BA2C as well as 0403:6010, and - when the firmware reports
bcdDevice 0x0102 - sets the STV0910 to serial TS output. Upstream longmynd
(last change 2022) does neither; BATC carry the change in their own copies:
portsdown5 src/longmynd (commit b5a2bfb, 7 October 2025), portsdown4 and
ryde-build. This is that change and nothing else from those copies (they also
add a search-algorithm option and an SR offset correction, which would change
how a MiniTiouner behaves on this box), in upstream's formatting, and without
their reuse of err for the descriptor read, which could hide a failed claim.

The daemon recognises a patched binary by its "FTDI/Pico init" message.

patch -p1 inside the longmynd tree.

diff -ruN a/ftdi.c b/ftdi.c
--- a/ftdi.c	2026-10-03 23:12:36.491350044 +0100
+++ b/ftdi.c	2026-10-03 23:13:05.472213619 +0100
@@ -40,6 +40,10 @@
 
 #define FTDI_VID 0x0403
 #define FTDI_PID 0x6010
+/* BATC PicoTuner (g4eml/PicoTuner firmware): a Raspberry Pi Pico that speaks the */
+/* same MPSSE subset as the FT2232H, under the Raspberry Pi VID                    */
+#define PICO_VID 0x2E8A
+#define PICO_PID 0xBA2C
 
 #define FTDI_NUM_TRIES 10
 #define FTDI_STOP_START_REPEATS 4
@@ -512,16 +516,16 @@
 /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
     uint8_t err;
 
-    printf("Flow: FTDI init\n");
+    printf("Flow: FTDI/Pico init\n");
 
-    err=ftdi_usb_init_i2c(usb_bus, usb_addr, FTDI_VID, FTDI_PID);
+    err=ftdi_usb_init_i2c(usb_bus, usb_addr, FTDI_VID, FTDI_PID, PICO_VID, PICO_PID);
     if (err==ERROR_NONE) err=ftdi_usb_set_mpsse_mode_i2c();
-    if (err==ERROR_NONE) err=ftdi_usb_init_ts(usb_bus, usb_addr, FTDI_VID, FTDI_PID);
+    if (err==ERROR_NONE) err=ftdi_usb_init_ts(usb_bus, usb_addr, FTDI_VID, FTDI_PID, PICO_VID, PICO_PID);
     if (err==ERROR_NONE) err=ftdi_usb_set_mpsse_mode_ts();
     if (err==ERROR_NONE) err=ftdi_setup_ftdi_io();
     if (err==ERROR_NONE) err=ftdi_nim_reset();
     
-    if (err!=ERROR_NONE) printf("ERROR: FTDI init\n");
+    if (err!=ERROR_NONE) printf("ERROR: FTDI/Pico init\n");
 
     return err;
 }
